# WSK-17 — the proof-rebuild site's DERIVED artifacts. Deliberately untracked.
#
# This site exists to prove one thing: that a real site can be rebuilt purely from the generated
# SDK plus the shared blocks package. So the generated inputs are, by definition, outputs of the
# rail — not source. Committing them would freeze a snapshot of the rail's output next to the lock
# that is supposed to determine it, and the two would drift silently. That is the same failure the
# program already guards against for docs/MAP.md ("generated from the filesystem ... if it
# disagrees with the repo, regenerate it — never hand-patch it").
#
# What IS tracked, and should be: CONTRACT.lock and CONTENT-CONTRACT.md (the pinned contract this
# site builds against), plus the site's own source. Everything below is reproducible from those by
# running the rail — see README.md and scripts/.
#
# Practical reason this file exists at all: these four paths showed up as untracked in a shared
# checkout that several agent sessions write to, which made a genuine "is anything unpushed?" check
# require sifting them out of 242 phantom entries. Untracked build output in a shared tree is not
# free; it costs the next person a search.

# Generated contract artifacts (produced by webdesk/api's codegen — WSK-15)
/openapi.v1.json
/hash-manifest.json
/src/sdk/

# The shared blocks package, vendored as a tarball at build time (WSK-16). A binary blob whose
# canonical source is webdesk/blocks; `npm pack`ed on demand, never reviewed as a diff.
/vendor/

# Astro/Node build output
/dist/
/.astro/
/node_modules/
